{"id":"u-a09574db-35e4-4000-bb79-1427bd6d95a9","src":"community","title":"Doosins 3day","author":"Johnny T.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/cpdZl7-power-jorts","desc":"Old dude 3day full body program to get eternally jacked and survive the hell scape of the manufacturing world. \n\nIt's impossible to know how much wrench turning or ladder climbing will be required on a day-to-day basis as a skilled trades worker. This is my solution for accommodating that extra volume and joint stress. \n\n1 Full body workout every 72 hours. ALWAYS 72 hours rest. With this setup, a 5 week program is actually just over 6 weeks time.\n\nEach workout starts with a main lift. The main lift is purposely programmed as the strength focus with lower volume for better recovery. Start with a weight that's an RPE 8 at 5 reps. If you can hit at least 3 clean reps for each set, increase the weight by a small amount next workout for that lift. Use double progression for the accessory work. \n\nWeek 5 is deload. Do the main lifts as 3 sets of 3 at RPE 7-8 and pick 2 accessory lifts.  \n\nKeep the progression SLOW for everything in general. You're old, bro. This program will build size and strength ,but the focus is longevity and recovery.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-15T19:55:45.488Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Safety Bar Squat","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":7,"x":2},{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":2},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9},{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9},{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9